# Pin Constraint File (PCF) for ice40-up5k FPGA
# This file maps logical signals to physical FPGA pins
#
# Board: iCEBreaker (default)
# Adjust pin numbers for your specific board:
#   - iCEBreaker: Use pins as shown below
#   - UPduino v3: CLK=20, LED=41, BTN=25 (or use GPIO)
#
# NOTE: iCEstick uses ice40-hx1k, NOT ice40-up5k, so it requires
# a completely different project configuration and is not compatible.

# ====================
# Clock Input (12 MHz)
# ====================
# Most ice40-up5k boards have a 12MHz oscillator
set_io clk 35  # iCEBreaker 12MHz clock

# ====================
# Reset Button
# ====================
# Active high reset button
# Note: You may need to add external pull-up/pull-down depending on your board
set_io reset 10  # iCEBreaker BTN1 (or use BTN2: pin 19, BTN3: pin 20)

# ====================
# LED Output
# ====================
# LED driven by bit 9 of the counter
set_io led 11  # iCEBreaker LED1 (LEDR_N)
# Other iCEBreaker LEDs available:
#   LED2 (LEDG_N): pin 37
#   LED3: pin 26
#   LED4: pin 27
#   LED5: pin 25

# ====================
# Alternative Pin Assignments
# ====================
# Uncomment and modify for your board:

# UPduino v3.0/3.1:
# set_io clk 20
# set_io reset 25
# set_io led 41

# ====================
# Notes for Beginners
# ====================
# 1. Pin numbers refer to physical FPGA package pins, not board headers
# 2. Consult your board's schematic/pinout diagram
# 3. Some LEDs may be active-low (invert in Verilog if needed)
# 4. Buttons may need debouncing for complex designs (not needed here)
# 5. Always verify your board's voltage levels (ice40-up5k is 3.3V)
